#   `pool_host` is moved into `engine_tool_host` under cfg(test-hooks) by a clone, so it is still usable here. `b.host` is the Arc<dyn HostChannel>
#   the engine host commands were built over (`serves(BrowserEngine)` decides engine or `host/browser/command`).
#   BridgeApprovalGates (a trait of the module: `fn gate(&self, session: &str) -> Option<Arc<dyn ApprovalGate>>`): the approval gate of the
#   session a bridge command runs in. For a session the core hosts it is that thread's session port put through `RunApprovals::gate_for`
#   (as the turn's own tool calls are); a session the core does not host has none, and the step is answered "approval required but no
#   approval UI is available" as for any step with no one to ask. The lead decides the source of the gate when applying this line; a
#   `struct NoGates; impl BridgeApprovalGates for NoGates { fn gate(&self, _: &str) -> Option<Arc<dyn ApprovalGate>> { None } }` in
#   compose_browser_engine.rs is the floor.

